# Testing and Observability

## Testing (when code exists / tests are authorized)

Distinguish: unit, integration, database integration, API contract, invariant, regression, security tests.

For financial / transactional behavior prioritize:

```text
invariants + failure cases + idempotency + state transitions
```

not only happy paths.

## Absolute

- Never report a test as passing unless it was actually executed
- Never weaken/delete tests merely to make CI pass
- Never claim production readiness merely because tests pass
- A failing test is evidence of a problem until proven otherwise

## Observability (when runtime is authorized)

- Structured logging
- Tracing where appropriate
- Preserve correlation / request identifiers
- Never log secrets or unnecessary sensitive financial/PII data
- Make transaction lifecycle and failures diagnosable

Observability must not become a sensitive-data leak channel.
